From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:14:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 213/213] feat: volumetric clouds in ray traced reflections
 (decision 09 section 9.2)

A reflection ray that misses above the horizon now marches the volumetric cloud
layer before it reads the sky dome, so a mirror facing the sky shows the clouds
the camera sees, in the right place, drifting with the same wind.

WHY A SECOND MARCH. CVolumetricCloudsStage::Execute runs at
StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:544, after the SVO block at :460, and it renders
into a screen space target: the only cloud image that exists is the sky the
CAMERA saw in that pixel, which is not what a reflected ray is looking at. So
the density field is evaluated again along the reflected direction, out of the
functions Clouds.cfx itself uses (CloudsCommon.cfi, factored out in 0cf232d6).

WHAT IS FRESH AT :460. ExecuteShadowGen() is called at :457-458, three lines
before SVOGI, so the tiled cloud shadow volume (x = optical thickness along the
sun, y = to the top of the layer, z = to the bottom) is THIS frame's. That is
exactly the sun transmittance source decision 09 section 9.2 asked for, and it
costs one tap per march step. Outside its tiling region the shader falls back to
a 3 step light march along the sun direction plus the analytic to-top /
to-bottom thickness - the !inShadowTex branch of GetOpticalThicknessCombined.

THE MARCH (Total_Illumination_Shading.cfi, SVO_RT_MarchClouds). N =
e_svoTI_RT_CloudSteps steps (default 12, clamped 1..64) between the ray's entry
into the spherical layer and its exit, distributed by vcGetLinearDepth exactly
as the direct view distributes its own, no jitter (the RT path has its own
temporal accumulation and a second dither would fight it). Per step one
GetCloudDensity and one shadow tap, then the arithmetic of Clouds.cfx's
AccumulateRadiance verbatim: Beer for the sun, the multi scatter preservation
lerp for the sky and ground terms, the powder effect on the sum, the precise
in-scattering integral. Early out below 0.01 transmittance; a zero density step
costs only its density taps.

COMPOSITE AND EXPOSURE. acc = sky * cloudTransmittance + cloudInscatter, on the
exposed side of ShadePS, before its single divide - the same convention the sky
lookup uses. Verified rather than assumed: GenerateCloudShaderParam multiplies
shadeColorFromSun (VolumetricClouds.cpp:1486) and skylightRayleighInScatter
(:1518) by GetSceneReferredExposure() and deliberately leaves the scattering and
extinction COEFFICIENTS alone because they live inside exp();
SetupShadeCloudConstants repeats exactly those two multiplies and scales nothing
else.

ANIMATION. The wind offset is PF.pVolCloudTilingOffset with the layer altitude
folded into z, the same lane the direct view uses, so a cloud drifts identically
in the mirror and in the sky.

BINDINGS. t51 noise, t52 edge noise, t53 cloud shadow volume, t54 Mie phase LUT;
s4 trilinear wrap, s5 trilinear border. All free on the ShadePass technique
(the forward stack tops out at t49, stage 5E took t41 and t50) and confirmed in
the compiled disassembly. Seventeen new SVO_Cloud* float4 constants, rebuilt
from the same E3DPARAM_VOLCLOUD_* globals and render view constants the stage
reads, because the stage's own values live in an inline b3 buffer filled after
us at a slot ShadePass already uses.

NOT CARRIED, deliberately: the atmospheric Rayleigh haze between the viewer and
the deck (the sky lookup already carries the dome's aerial perspective; adding
the cloud pass's copy would count it twice), the cirrus layer, the stereo
reprojection, and the sky-ray edge fade of decisions/s9-cloud-edge.md (it hides
a seam caused by camera-space march limits a reflection ray does not have).

Also here, one line each in SceneTreeCVars.inl: the two new cvars, and the
e_svoTI_RT_Debug help entries for views 16-21, which had been left out while
that file was busy (report 05e gap 1).

  e_svoTI_RT_Clouds      1   march the layer on a miss above the horizon
  e_svoTI_RT_CloudSteps  12  steps through the layer
  e_svoTI_RT_Debug 20        cloud in-scatter, exposed radiance
  e_svoTI_RT_Debug 21        cloud transmittance - the cloud's shape

Native path: every shader hunk is inside %_RT_QUALITY, every C++ hunk is behind
e_svoTI_RT_Active, and the frame order is untouched. With clouds unbound
SVO_CloudParams0.x is 0, the march returns immediately, transmittance is 1 and
in-scatter is 0, so the miss path is the bare sky lookup it was at 3f33313a.
The two cvar mirrors are resolved defensively (a null ICVar keeps the header
default), as the glossy knobs are.

Validation: cryfx_lint.py 0 findings on the five owned shader files;
rtharness2/validate.sh 17 fxc compiles, 0 errors; ShadePS disassembled with
%_RT_SAMPLE3 forced on to prove CloudBaseDensityTexture never reaches this
technique; CryRenderD3D11 and Cry3DEngine Profile, 0 errors 0 warnings outside
Code/SDKs. No engine run, no deploy.

